  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global: Local Voices, Global Networks: Women&#x2019;s Voices Shaping Multi-Stakeholder Engagements on Gender, Human Rights and Rule of Law</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To hold events and targeted meetings for field-based practitioners to engage with Geneva-based actors, including gender and rule of law experts, researchers and academics, policymakers, government officials, human rights advocates, thereby enhancing the connectivity between Geneva and the field and the effectiveness of those working to eliminate discriminatory laws and advance survivor-centred justice for gender-based violence in complex situations. 2) To bolster advocacy over the longer term and foster strengthened networks comprised of experts dedicated to addressing gender equality and rule of law challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Practitioners from the national level and Geneva-based institutions and actors, including gender and rule of law experts, researchers and academics, policymakers, government officials, human rights advocates, young women and community leaders.Indirect beneficiaries: Women and girls.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to strengthen multi-stakeholder and multi-level engagements at the intersection of gender, human rights, and the rule of law by connecting national-level practitioners at the forefront of the work on gender-based violence and eliminating discriminatory laws with Geneva-based actors that can support transformative changes on the ground.</narrative>
  </description>
